# The Challenger - settings
#
# Copy to `challenger.conf` (same folder as challenger_hook.py) and edit.
# Settings only: no credentials live here. Both editor backends authenticate
# through their own CLI (`codex login`, or whatever Claude Code already uses).
#
# This file is gitignored, so `git pull` never touches your setup. Values are
# read into the environment, so a real environment variable wins over the file
# and any setting can be overridden for a single run.


# --- Which projects get edited (the one setting you must set) ----------------
#
# Absolute project roots, separated by your platform's path separator
# (";" on Windows, ":" on macOS/Linux). A session is edited when its working
# directory is one of these roots or anything beneath it, so git worktrees are
# covered automatically. With this unset the Challenger is installed but inert.
#
# Everything outside these roots is waved through in ~70ms, which is why the
# hook can safely be registered globally.

CHALLENGER_PROJECTS=C:\code\my-project;C:\code\another-project
# CHALLENGER_PROJECTS=/home/me/code/my-project:/home/me/code/another-project


# --- Which model does the editing -------------------------------------------
#
# "codex" (default) runs OpenAI's gpt-5.6-sol through the vendored bridge and
# needs the Codex CLI installed and logged in. An editor from a different
# vendor does not share the stylistic habits of the model it is editing.
#
# "claude" runs `claude -p` with claude-fable-5 and needs nothing extra.

# CHALLENGER_CRITIC=claude


# --- Your own house style ----------------------------------------------------
#
# critic-prompt.md is tracked, so editing it in place will conflict on your next
# update. To customise the register of your reports, copy it alongside as
# critic-prompt.local.md (gitignored) and point this at it:

# CHALLENGER_PROMPT=critic-prompt.local.md


# --- Tuning ------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The defaults below are the tested ones; change them only if something about
# the behaviour bothers you. Full explanations are in README.md.

# CHALLENGER_MIN_CHARS=1000            # shorter responses are never edited
# CHALLENGER_TARGET_MODEL=claude-opus-5 # model prefix to edit; "claude-" for all
# CHALLENGER_MAX_ASK_ROUNDS=2          # editor clarification rounds before giving up
# CHALLENGER_TIMEOUT=300               # seconds; stay under the hook timeout (360)
# CHALLENGER_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol
# CHALLENGER_CODEX_EFFORT=high
# CHALLENGER_CODEX_BRIDGE=vendor/ask_codex.py
# CHALLENGER_CRITIC_MODEL=claude-fable-5  # claude backend
# CHALLENGER_CLAUDE_BIN=claude
# CHALLENGER_LOG=hook-debug.log
